+---
+id: task-001-newsletter-discount-codes-spring10-and-welcome5
+type: task
+title: "Newsletter discount codes SPRING10 and WELCOME5"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Request
+
+The spring campaign sends discount codes in the newsletter. An order takes a code:
+
+- `SPRING10`: 10 % off the order's items, rounded to the nearest cent (a half cent rounds up).
+- `WELCOME5`: 5.00 € (500 cents) off the order's items, only on an order whose items come to 30.00 € (3000 cents) or more.
+
+An order takes one code at most; a second code replaces the first. An unknown code, or `WELCOME5` on a smaller
+order, is refused with an error that says why, and the order is left as it was. The discount never touches
+shipping. Whether an order ships free is still decided on its items before any discount.
+
+The order book offers `applyCode(orderNumber, code)`. An order's totals show `discountCents` (0 without a code),
+and `totalCents` is items minus discount plus shipping.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- `applyCode` on an existing order with a valid code stores it; a later code replaces it.
+- `applyCode` refuses an unknown order, an unknown code, and `WELCOME5` below 3000 cents of items, with a message
+  that says why; a refused call leaves the order's code and totals unchanged.
+- `SPRING10` rounds half cents up (for example, 5 cents of items gives 1 cent off, since 0.5 rounds up).
+- Totals: `discountCents` is 0 with no code; `totalCents` = `itemsCents` - `discountCents` + `shippingCents`.
+- Shipping is charged or waived on the items before discount, so a discount never changes shipping.
+- Existing behaviour and tests keep passing; the new behaviour has tests.
+
+## Plan
+
+- New module `src/domain/discounts.ts` with the two codes and their rules, in integer cents.
+- `OrderBook` gains `applyCode`; `OrderTotals` gains `discountCents`. Codes are matched after trimming and
+  upper-casing, so `spring10` works too.
+- No version bump or CHANGELOG entry: that waits for the approver (directive p1).
+
+## Done
+
+- Built test-first: nine discount tests in `test/shop.test.ts` (`discount codes`) went red on
+  `applyCode is not a function`, then passed. The order-book test's totals now include `discountCents: 0`.
+- `src/domain/discounts.ts`: `discountFor(code, itemsCents)`, integer rounding `floor((items * 10 + 50) / 100)`
+  for SPRING10, and the WELCOME5 minimum of 3000 cents with a refusal message that gives the items total.
+- `src/domain/orders.ts`: `applyCode(number, code)` stores the code per order only when it is accepted, so a
+  refused call changes nothing; `totals` and `applyCode` share `totalsOf`, which takes shipping on the
+  pre-discount items.
+- `npm test`: 14 pass, 0 fail. Type-checking was not run (no `tsc` installed); types were checked by reading.
+- Not done here: CHANGELOG entry and version bump, which wait for the approver (directive p1).
